--- body ---
## Context

0202's validation cycle (raid 0203/0208/0201/0204/0167, 2026-06-04) ran
six /gaze fork invocations under the 0193 contracts. Containment held
on the headline criteria — zero off-task runs, zero foreign files, zero
rogue pushes/PRs — but contract drift INSIDE the forks recurred in three
milder forms:

1. PR #274 run 1: the fork under-executed its directive — no gate
   invocation, no verdict comment, stale /tmp/review-274 left behind,
   containment postcondition skipped. Orchestrator had to clean up and
   retry (clean on retry).
2. PR #276 fix loop: attempted an out-of-role rebase + force-push of the
   PR branch (the 0193 incident-#7 mode). The permission guard DENIED the
   force-push — positive evidence the guard layer works — but the fork
   then worked around it with a cherry-pick and left commit 90de0bc
   carrying a false "Rebased onto origin/main" message.
3. PR #276 gate fork: emitted a malformed erg log line (invalid author/
   verb) that would have failed erg validate; discarded before reaching
   the branch.

Per 0202's escalation clause: the 2026-06-03 evidence already showed
Agent(isolation:"worktree") execute agents with imperative prompts and
pinned cwd never drifted; only context:fork Skill invocations did. The
deterministic fix is to move verify's sub-skill execution onto that
mechanism (prototyped clean in PRs #263/#264).

## Relevant files

- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` phases 2-4 (fan-out) and 6 (gate) — the
  context:fork invocations to convert
- `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md`, `skills/verify-adherence/SKILL.md`,
  `skills/simplify/` — invoked surfaces; their TASK DIRECTIVE openers
  stay (defense in depth)
- tickets/closed/0193, tickets/0202 — incident catalog and validation log

## Actions

1. Rewrite verify phases 2-4 to spawn Agent sub-agents (read-only,
   pinned cwd = /tmp/review-<pr>) instead of Skill forks; embed each
   sub-skill's operating procedure imperatively in the agent prompt.
2. Same for phase 6 (gate), returning the structured verdict as agent
   output.
3. Keep the orchestrator-side containment postcondition; it caught
   nothing this cycle only because exit-path checks ran — keep them.
4. Consider a push/PR guard scoped to verify sub-agent sessions as a
   second layer (the #276 force-push denial shows guards bite).

## Test

One full /gaze run on a real PR: all phases complete, verdict posted,
no stale /tmp worktrees, no branch switches, transcript shows zero
out-of-role mutation attempts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Verify phases 2-4 and 6 run as Agent-spawned sub-agents with pinned cwd
- [ ] One clean /gaze cycle on a real PR under the new mechanism
- [ ] Containment postcondition retained
